## Bug #1 (docs/specs/syntax/async_lowering.spec.md): a `.await` inside
## an enum-variant constructor argument (`Option.Some(make_int().await)`)
## must be seen by the await-scan so the fn takes the await-aware
## lowering path. Before the Visit migration, `expr_contains_await`
## had a `_ => false` arm that missed `ExprKind::EnumVariant`, so the
## fn fell into the no-await path and the resolver then misreported
## E1110 ("`.await` only valid inside async def") on a `.await` that
## is, in fact, inside an async def.

async def make_int() -> Int
  42
end

async def f() -> Option[Int]
  let x = Option.Some(make_int().await)
  x
end
